        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "963b1398-22fb-51e9-bf07-ab483d995519",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Roy Dotrice, Robin Midgley, David Warner, Peggy Ashcroft, Donald Sinden, Paul Hardwick, Janet Suzman, Brewster Mason, Susan Engel, Ian Holm\n- Works: The Wars of the Roses, A Moon for the Misbegotten, Z-Cars\n- Organizations: Royal Shakespeare Company\n- Roles: Henry VI, Margaret of Anjou, Duke of York, Duke of Gloucester, Joan la Pucelle, Earl of Warwick, Edward IV, Queen Elizabeth, Richard III\n\nFacts:\n- Roy Dotrice was born on 26 May 1923 and became a British actor.\n- Robin Midgley was born on 10 November 1934 and became a director in theatre, television, and radio.\n- Roy Dotrice was known for his Tony Award-winning Broadway performance in the revival of A Moon for the Misbegotten.\n- Robin Midgley was responsible for some of the earliest episodes of Z-Cars.\n- The production The Wars of the Roses starred David Warner as Henry VI, Peggy Ashcroft as Margaret of Anjou, Donald Sinden as the Duke of York, Paul Hardwick as the Duke of Gloucester, Janet Suzman as Joan la Pucelle, Brewster Mason as the Earl of Warwick, Roy Dotrice as Edward IV, Susan Engel as Queen Elizabeth, and Ian Holm as Richard III.\n- Robin Midgley was responsible for the television version of the Royal Shakespeare Company's The Wars of the Roses.\n- Robin Midgley died on 19 May 2007.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "58c1b2aa-f406-55a3-865b-0c251d331573",
        "text": "Page: The Wars of the Roses (adaptation). Sentence: The production starred David Warner as Henry VI, Peggy Ashcroft as Margaret of Anjou, Donald Sinden as the Duke of York, Paul Hardwick as the Duke of Gloucester, Janet Suzman as Joan la Pucelle, Brewster Mason as the Earl of Warwick, Roy Dotrice as Edward IV, Susan Engel as Queen Elizabeth and Ian Holm as Richard III.\nPage: Roy Dotrice. Sentence: Roy Dotrice, OBE (born 26 May 1923) is a British actor known for his Tony Award-winning Broadway performance in the revival of \"A Moon for the Misbegotten\".\nPage: Robin Midgley. Sentence: Robin Midgley (10 November 1934 – 19 May 2007) was a director in theatre, television and radio and responsible for some of the earliest episodes of \"Z-Cars\" and for the television version of the Royal Shakespeare Company's \"Wars of the Roses\".",
